-- coa11-part16-ch2-private.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 16 (Audit), Chapter 2 (Appointment of auditors),
-- the cross-heading "Private companies": ss 485 to 488 (with 485A, 485B, 485C, 486A and 487A): raw lines 6698-6796.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no seat, no point of view.  Reading a result, the polarity of names, inputs: as in
-- coa11-part16-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE with a FALSE-kind comment / NOTHING with a NOTHING-kind comment).
-- Periods are counted as fork F6 in NOTES.md says: "the period of 28 days beginning with X" is X to X plus 27 days;
-- "within one week of" a day is that day to that day plus 7, both ends inclusive; "4 years beginning with the day after
-- D" ends on the day before the fourth anniversary of the day after D.
-- Every top-level name, type, constructor and field begins with the label of the provision it implements.

§ `Part 16 Chapter 2: Appointment of auditors: private companies (ss 485 to 488)`

§§ `s 485 Appointment of auditors of private company: general`

-- src:6701 | (1) An auditor or auditors of a private company must be appointed for each financial year of the company, unless the directors reasonably resolve otherwise on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required.
@ref s 485(1) An auditor must be appointed for each financial year (src:6701-6701)
GIVEN `the company is a private company (section 4(1))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed for the financial year on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors' resolution was a reasonable one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company is a private company (section 4(1))`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor or auditors of a private company"
        IF `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed for the financial year on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required` AND `the directors' resolution was a reasonable one`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the directors reasonably resolve otherwise on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required" (the unless is met: fork F3)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6702 | (2) For each financial year for which an auditor or auditors is or are to be appointed (other than the company's first financial year), the appointment must be made before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with—
-- src:6703 | (a) the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year (see section 424), or
-- src:6704 | (b) if earlier, the day on which copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are sent out under section 423.
-- src:6705 | This is the “period for appointing auditors”.
@ref s 485(2) The period for appointing auditors (src:6702-6705)
DECLARE `s 485(2) period for appointing auditors` HAS
    `s 485(2) first day of the period for appointing auditors` IS A DATE
    `s 485(2) last day of the period for appointing auditors` IS A DATE

-- src:6702 | (2) For each financial year for which an auditor or auditors is or are to be appointed (other than the company's first financial year), the appointment must be made before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with—
-- src:6703 | (a) the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year (see section 424), or
-- src:6704 | (b) if earlier, the day on which copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are sent out under section 423.
-- src:6705 | This is the “period for appointing auditors”.
@ref s 485(2) The period for appointing auditors (src:6702-6705)
GIVEN `s 424 the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year` IS A DATE
      `s 423 the day on which copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are sent out` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `s 485(2) period for appointing auditors`
`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` MEANS
    `s 485(2) period for appointing auditors` OF first, `s 485(2) the last day of the 28 days beginning with` first
    WHERE
        -- "(a) the end of the time allowed ..., or (b) if earlier, the day on which copies ... are sent out under section 423"
        first MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 423 the day on which copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are sent out`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 424 the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year`
            WHEN JUST sent THEN
                IF sent LESS THAN `s 424 the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year`
                THEN sent
                ELSE `s 424 the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year`

-- src:6702 | (2) For each financial year for which an auditor or auditors is or are to be appointed (other than the company's first financial year), the appointment must be made before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with—
-- src:6703 | (a) the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year (see section 424), or
-- src:6704 | (b) if earlier, the day on which copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are sent out under section 423.
-- src:6705 | This is the “period for appointing auditors”.
@ref s 485(2) The period of 28 days beginning with (src:6702-6705)
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 485(2) the last day of the 28 days beginning with` MEANS
    Date (Day `the first day` PLUS 27) -- "the period of 28 days beginning with" the first day: that day is day 1 of 28 (fork F6)

-- src:6702 | (2) For each financial year for which an auditor or auditors is or are to be appointed (other than the company's first financial year), the appointment must be made before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with—
-- src:6703 | (a) the end of the time allowed for sending out copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year (see section 424), or
-- src:6704 | (b) if earlier, the day on which copies of the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are sent out under section 423.
-- src:6705 | This is the “period for appointing auditors”.
@ref s 485(2) The appointment must be made before the end of the period (src:6702-6705)
GIVEN `the appointment is for the company's first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      period IS A `s 485(2) period for appointing auditors`
      `the day the appointment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is for the company's first financial year`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than the company's first financial year)"
        IF `the day the appointment is made` AT MOST period's `s 485(2) last day of the period for appointing auditors`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the appointment must be made before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:6706 | (3) The directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company—
-- src:6707 | (a) at any time before the company's first period for appointing auditors,
-- src:6708 | (b) following a period during which the company (being exempt from audit) did not have any auditor, at any time before the company's next period for appointing auditors, or
-- src:6709 | (c) to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor.
@ref s 485(3) The directors may appoint an auditor (src:6706-6709)
GIVEN `the appointment is made at any time before the company's first period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made following a period during which the company, being exempt from audit, did not have any auditor, at a time before the company's next period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` MEANS
    IF    `the appointment is made at any time before the company's first period for appointing auditors`
       OR `the appointment is made following a period during which the company, being exempt from audit, did not have any auditor, at a time before the company's next period for appointing auditors`
       OR `the appointment is made to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company— (a) at any time before ..., (b) following a period ..., or (c) to fill a casual vacancy": a grant that names its occasions; it does not say the directors may not appoint on another (fork F13)

-- src:6710 | (4) The members may appoint an auditor or auditors by ordinary resolution—
-- src:6711 | (a) during a period for appointing auditors,
-- src:6712 | (b) if the company should have appointed an auditor or auditors during a period for appointing auditors but failed to do so, or
-- src:6713 | (c) where the directors had power to appoint under subsection (3) but have failed to make an appointment.
@ref s 485(4) The members may appoint by ordinary resolution (src:6710-6713)
GIVEN `the appointment is made during a period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company should have appointed an auditor or auditors during a period for appointing auditors but failed to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors had power to appoint under subsection (3) but have failed to make an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `the appointment is made during a period for appointing auditors`
                OR `the company should have appointed an auditor or auditors during a period for appointing auditors but failed to do so`
                OR `the directors had power to appoint under subsection (3) but have failed to make an appointment`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members may appoint an auditor or auditors by ordinary resolution— (a) during a period for appointing auditors, (b) if ..., or (c) where ..."
        IF `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by ordinary resolution": the grant is of an appointment by that kind of resolution
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 282 is not known

-- src:6714 | (5) An auditor or auditors of a private company may only be appointed—
-- src:6715 | (a) in accordance with this section, or
-- src:6716 | (b) in accordance with section 486 or 486A (default power of Secretary of State).
-- src:6717 | This is without prejudice to any deemed re-appointment under section 487.
@ref s 485(5) Only in accordance with this section, section 486 or section 486A (src:6714-6717)
GIVEN `the appointment is made in accordance with section 485` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made in accordance with section 486 or 486A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is a deemed re-appointment under section 487` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is a deemed re-appointment under section 487`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is without prejudice to any deemed re-appointment under section 487"
        IF `the appointment is made in accordance with section 485` OR `the appointment is made in accordance with section 486 or 486A`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "may only be appointed— (a) in accordance with this section, or (b) in accordance with section 486 or 486A": JUST TRUE says only that this subsection does not bar it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor or auditors of a private company may only be appointed— (a) in accordance with this section, or (b) in accordance with section 486 or 486A"

§§ `s 485A Appointment of auditors of private company: additional requirements for public interest entities with audit committees`

-- The text shows omitted words as "..." in s 485A(3)(b) and (4) (finding 2); the encoding follows the words as shown.

-- src:6719 | (1) This section applies to the appointment under section 485(4) of an auditor or auditors of a private company—
-- src:6720 | (a) which is also a public interest entity; and
-- src:6721 | (b) which has an audit committee.
-- src:6722 | (2) But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company.
@ref s 485A(1) and (2) Where the section applies (src:6719-6722)
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company (section 4(1))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 494A the company has an audit committee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company (section 494A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company (section 494A)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company"
        IF    `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` AND `the company is a private company (section 4(1))`
          AND `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `s 494A the company has an audit committee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 494A the company has an audit committee` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a public interest entity, or has an audit committee, is not known
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to the appointment under section 485(4) of an auditor or auditors of a private company— (a) which is also a public interest entity; and (b) which has an audit committee": a scope with no "only" (fork F14)

DECLARE `s 485A party` IS ONE OF
    `s 485A the audit committee`
    `s 485A the directors`

DECLARE `s 485A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 485A(3)(a) make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment`
    `s 485A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment`

-- src:6723 | (3) Before an appointment to which this section applies is made—
-- src:6724 | (a) the audit committee of the company must make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment, and
-- src:6725 | (b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment ...
@ref s 485A(3)(a) Before an appointment the audit committee must make a recommendation (src:6723-6725)
GIVEN `the number of days before the appointment is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 485A party` `s 485A act`
`s 485A(3)(a) the audit committee must make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment is made` MEANS
    PARTY `s 485A the audit committee`
    MUST `s 485A(3)(a) make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment`
    WITHIN `the number of days before the appointment is made`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 485A the audit committee` BECAUSE "s 485A(3)(a): the audit committee did not make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment was made"

-- src:6723 | (3) Before an appointment to which this section applies is made—
-- src:6724 | (a) the audit committee of the company must make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment, and
-- src:6725 | (b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment ...
@ref s 485A(3)(b) Before an appointment the directors must propose an auditor or auditors (src:6723-6725)
GIVEN `the number of days before the appointment is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 485A party` `s 485A act`
`s 485A(3)(b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` MEANS
    PARTY `s 485A the directors`
    MUST `s 485A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment`
    WITHIN `the number of days before the appointment is made`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 485A the directors` BECAUSE "s 485A(3)(b): the directors did not propose an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made"

-- src:6723 | (3) Before an appointment to which this section applies is made—
-- src:6724 | (a) the audit committee of the company must make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment, and
-- src:6725 | (b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment ...
@ref s 485A(3) Before an appointment to which this section applies is made (src:6723-6725)
GIVEN `the appointment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit committee made its recommendation before the appointment was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors made their proposal before the appointment was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appointment has been made`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before an appointment to which this section applies is made": the time for both steps has not yet run
        IF `the audit committee made its recommendation before the appointment was made` AND `the directors made their proposal before the appointment was made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before an appointment to which this section applies is made— (a) the audit committee of the company must make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment, and (b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment" (a bare must not done: fork F4)

-- src:6726 | (4) Before the audit committee makes a recommendation or the directors make a proposal under subsection (3), the committee ... must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation , unless the company is a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC .
@ref s 485A(4) The selection procedure (src:6726-6726)
-- src:6738 | (7) Where the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company’s existing auditor or auditors, and the directors are in agreement, subsections (4) and (5)(a) and (b) do not apply.
@ref s 485A(7) Re-appointment (src:6738-6738)
GIVEN `section 485A(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors and the directors are in agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 485A(1) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General"
        IF `the company is a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the company is a small or medium sized enterprise within the meaning in Article 2(1)(f) of Directive 2003/71/EC" (the unless is met: fork F3)
        IF `the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors and the directors are in agreement`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors, and the directors are in agreement, subsections (4) and (5)(a) and (b) do not apply" (subsection (7))
        IF `section 485A(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 485A does not apply to this appointment on the facts known

-- src:6727 | (5) The audit committee must in its recommendation—
-- src:6728 | (a) identify its first and second choice candidates for appointment, drawn from those auditors who have participated in a selection procedure under subsection (4),
-- src:6729 | (b) give reasons for the choices so identified,
-- src:6730 | (c) state that—
-- src:6731 | (i) the recommendation is free from influence by a third party, and
-- src:6732 | (ii) no contractual term of the kind mentioned in Article 16(6) of the Audit Regulation has been imposed on the company.
@ref s 485A(5) What the recommendation must contain (src:6727-6732)
-- src:6738 | (7) Where the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company’s existing auditor or auditors, and the directors are in agreement, subsections (4) and (5)(a) and (b) do not apply.
@ref s 485A(7) Re-appointment (src:6738-6738)
GIVEN `the recommendation identifies its first and second choice candidates for appointment, drawn from those auditors who have participated in a selection procedure under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recommendation gives reasons for the choices so identified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recommendation states that it is free from influence by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recommendation states that no contractual term of the kind mentioned in Article 16(6) of the Audit Regulation has been imposed on the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors and the directors are in agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` MEANS
    IF    `the recommendation states that it is free from influence by a third party`
      AND `the recommendation states that no contractual term of the kind mentioned in Article 16(6) of the Audit Regulation has been imposed on the company`
      AND (   `the audit committee recommends re-appointment of the company's existing auditor or auditors and the directors are in agreement`
           OR (    `the recommendation identifies its first and second choice candidates for appointment, drawn from those auditors who have participated in a selection procedure under subsection (4)`
               AND `the recommendation gives reasons for the choices so identified`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The audit committee must in its recommendation— (a) identify its first and second choice candidates ..., (b) give reasons ..., (c) state that— (i) ... and (ii) ..." (a bare must not done: fork F4; limbs (a) and (b) fall away under subsection (7))

-- src:6733 | (6) The directors must include in their proposal—
-- src:6734 | (a) the recommendation made by the audit committee in connection with the appointment, and
-- src:6735 | (b) if the proposal of the directors departs from the preference of the audit committee—
-- src:6736 | (i) a recommendation for a candidate or candidates for appointment drawn from those auditors who have participated in a selection procedure under subsection (4), and
-- src:6737 | (ii) the reasons for not following the audit committee’s recommendation.
@ref s 485A(6) What the directors' proposal must contain (src:6733-6737)
GIVEN `the proposal includes the recommendation made by the audit committee in connection with the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal of the directors departs from the preference of the audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal includes a recommendation for a candidate or candidates drawn from those auditors who have participated in a selection procedure under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal includes the reasons for not following the audit committee's recommendation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` MEANS
    IF    `the proposal includes the recommendation made by the audit committee in connection with the appointment`
      AND (    (NOT `the proposal of the directors departs from the preference of the audit committee`)
            OR (    `the proposal includes a recommendation for a candidate or candidates drawn from those auditors who have participated in a selection procedure under subsection (4)`
                AND `the proposal includes the reasons for not following the audit committee's recommendation`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must include in their proposal— (a) the recommendation made by the audit committee in connection with the appointment, and (b) if the proposal of the directors departs from the preference of the audit committee— (i) ... and (ii) ..." (a bare must not done: fork F4)

§§ `s 485B Appointment of auditors of private company: additional requirements for public interest entities without audit committees`

-- src:6740 | (1) This section applies to the appointment under section 485(4) of an auditor or auditors of a private company—
-- src:6741 | (a) which is also a public interest entity; and
-- src:6742 | (b) which does not have an audit committee.
-- src:6743 | (2) But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company.
@ref s 485B(1) and (2) Where the section applies (src:6740-6743)
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company (section 4(1))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 494A the company has an audit committee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company (section 494A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company (section 494A)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company"
        IF    `the appointment is made under section 485(4)` AND `the company is a private company (section 4(1))`
          AND `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `s 494A the company has an audit committee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 494A the company has an audit committee` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a public interest entity, or has an audit committee, is not known
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to the appointment under section 485(4) of an auditor or auditors of a private company— (a) which is also a public interest entity; and (b) which does not have an audit committee": a scope with no "only" (fork F14)

DECLARE `s 485B party` IS ONE OF
