-- src:6769 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 486A(6) Liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale (src:6769-6769)
GIVEN `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 486A(6) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

-- src:6769 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 486A(6) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 (src:6769-6769)
GIVEN `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 486A(6) the most the person can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount of level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` TIMES 0.1

§§ `s 487 Term of office of auditors of private company`

-- s 487(1A) to (1E) are shown blank in the text; s 487A is shown blank (coverage table: repealed or blank).

-- src:6772 | (a) they do not take office until any previous auditor or auditors cease to hold office, and
@ref s 487(1)(a) They do not take office until any previous auditor or auditors cease to hold office (src:6772-6772)
GIVEN `a previous auditor or auditors still hold office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(1)(a) the auditor or auditors cannot yet take office` MEANS
    IF `a previous auditor or auditors still hold office`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "they do not take office until any previous auditor or auditors cease to hold office": the bar holds before that time
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not take office until any previous auditor or auditors cease to hold office": the previous auditors have ceased (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d))

-- src:6773 | (b) they cease to hold office at the end of the next period for appointing auditors unless re-appointed.
@ref s 487(1)(b) They cease to hold office at the end of the next period for appointing auditors unless re-appointed (src:6773-6773)
GIVEN `the day now` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the next period for appointing auditors` IS A DATE
      `the auditor or auditors have been re-appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the auditor or auditors have been re-appointed`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they cease to hold office at the end of the next period for appointing auditors unless re-appointed"
        IF `the day now` GREATER THAN `the last day of the next period for appointing auditors`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they cease to hold office at the end of the next period for appointing auditors": that period has not yet ended (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:6779 | (2) Where no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors, any auditor in office immediately before that time is deemed to be re-appointed at that time, unless—
-- src:6780 | (a) he was appointed by the directors, or
-- src:6781 | (b) the company's articles require actual re-appointment, or
-- src:6782 | (c) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members under section 488, or
-- src:6783 | (d) the members have resolved that he should not be re-appointed, or
-- src:6784 | (e) the directors have resolved that no auditor or auditors should be appointed for the financial year in question or
-- src:6785 | (f) the auditor’s appointment would be in breach of section 485C.
@ref s 487(2) Deemed re-appointment (src:6779-6785)
GIVEN `no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an auditor was in office immediately before that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he was appointed by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles require actual re-appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 488(1) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the members have resolved that he should not be re-appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have resolved that no auditor or auditors should be appointed for the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 485C the auditor's appointment would be in breach of section 485C` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(2) the auditor in office is deemed to be re-appointed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors`) OR (NOT `an auditor was in office immediately before that time`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no auditor has been appointed by the end of the next period for appointing auditors, any auditor in office immediately before that time is deemed to be re-appointed" (a "where" that is not met: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F17)
        IF    `he was appointed by the directors`
           OR `the company's articles require actual re-appointment`
           OR `s 488(1) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `the members have resolved that he should not be re-appointed`
           OR `the directors have resolved that no auditor or auditors should be appointed for the financial year in question`
           OR `s 485C the auditor's appointment would be in breach of section 485C` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be re-appointed at that time, unless— (a) he was appointed by the directors, or (b) the company's articles require actual re-appointment, or (c) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members under section 488, or (d) the members have resolved that he should not be re-appointed, or (e) the directors have resolved that no auditor or auditors should be appointed for the financial year in question or (f) the auditor's appointment would be in breach of section 485C" (an unless that is met: fork F3)
        IF    `s 488(1) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          AND `s 485C the auditor's appointment would be in breach of section 485C` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 488 or section 485C answer is not known

-- src:6786 | (3) This is without prejudice to the provisions of this Part as to removal and resignation of auditors.
@ref s 487(3) Without prejudice to the provisions of this Part as to removal and resignation of auditors (src:6786-6786)
GIVEN `the provision is one of the provisions of Part 16 as to removal and resignation of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(3) the deemed re-appointment prejudices the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one of the provisions of Part 16 as to removal and resignation of auditors`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is without prejudice to the provisions of this Part as to removal and resignation of auditors"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving names only the provisions on removal and resignation

-- src:6787 | (4) No account shall be taken of any loss of the opportunity of deemed re-appointment under this section in ascertaining the amount of any compensation or damages payable to an auditor on his ceasing to hold office for any reason.
@ref s 487(4) No account shall be taken of any loss of the opportunity of deemed re-appointment (src:6787-6787)
GIVEN `the loss in question is loss of the opportunity of deemed re-appointment under section 487` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487(4) the loss is taken into account in ascertaining the compensation or damages payable to the auditor` MEANS
    IF `the loss in question is loss of the opportunity of deemed re-appointment under section 487`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No account shall be taken of any loss of the opportunity of deemed re-appointment under this section in ascertaining the amount of any compensation or damages payable to an auditor on his ceasing to hold office for any reason"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names only loss of that opportunity; the text says nothing of other losses

§§ `s 488 Prevention by members of deemed re-appointment of auditor`

-- src:6792 | (2) The “requisite percentage” is 5%, or such lower percentage as is specified for this purpose in the company's articles.
@ref s 488(2) The requisite percentage (src:6792-6792)
GIVEN `the percentage the company's articles specify for this purpose, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 488(2) the requisite percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the percentage the company's articles specify for this purpose, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 5%
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF specified LESS THAN 5%
        THEN specified -- "such lower percentage as is specified for this purpose in the company's articles"
        ELSE 5% -- a percentage that is not lower than 5% is not "such lower percentage" (fork F18)

-- src:6793 | (3) A notice under this section—
-- src:6794 | (a) may be in hard copy or electronic form,
-- src:6795 | (b) must be authenticated by the person or persons giving it, and
-- src:6796 | (c) must be received by the company before the end of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the time when the deemed re-appointment would have effect.
@ref s 488(3) A notice (src:6793-6796)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
      `the notice is authenticated by the person or persons giving it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company received the notice` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the time when the deemed re-appointment would have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488(3) the notice is a notice under section 488` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the notice is authenticated by the person or persons giving it`)
       OR `the day the company received the notice` GREATER THAN `the last day of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the time when the deemed re-appointment would have effect`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) must be authenticated by the person or persons giving it, and (c) must be received by the company before the end of the accounting reference period immediately preceding the time when the deemed re-appointment would have effect" (a bare must not done, and a period the text fixes in its own words: fork F4; a notice received on the last day counts, fork F6)
    ELSE CONSIDER form
         WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE -- "(a) may be in hard copy or electronic form"
         WHEN `electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:6791 | (1) An auditor of a private company is not deemed to be re-appointed under section 487(2) if the company has received notices under this section from members representing at least the requisite percentage of the total voting rights of all members who would be entitled to vote on a resolution that the auditor should not be re-appointed.
@ref s 488(1) An auditor of a private company is not deemed to be re-appointed if the company has received notices (src:6791-6791)
GIVEN `the fraction of the total voting rights of all members who would be entitled to vote on a resolution that the auditor should not be re-appointed, represented by the members who have given notices under section 488` IS A NUMBER
      `the requisite percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488(1) the deemed re-appointment is prevented by the members` MEANS
    IF `the fraction of the total voting rights of all members who would be entitled to vote on a resolution that the auditor should not be re-appointed, represented by the members who have given notices under section 488` AT LEAST `the requisite percentage`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "An auditor of a private company is not deemed to be re-appointed under section 487(2) if the company has received notices under this section from members representing at least the requisite percentage"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not deemed to be re-appointed under section 487(2) if the company has received notices under this section from members representing at least the requisite percentage": the bar does not catch it (an if that is not met)
